# Boogeyman 1 — Phishing, Endpoint and Network Forensics Investigation

## 1. Investigation Overview

This report documents an investigation of the TryHackMe Boogeyman 1 scenario, involving a targeted phishing attack against the finance department of Quick Logistics LLC.

The investigation follows the attack from a malicious email attachment through PowerShell execution, system enumeration, command-and-control (C2) communication, and the exfiltration of sensitive information.

### Objectives

- Investigate the phishing email and its attachment.
- Identify the malicious execution mechanism.
- Analyze PowerShell activity on the compromised workstation.
- Identify attacker-controlled infrastructure.
- Investigate HTTP-based command-and-control traffic.
- Detect and reconstruct DNS-based data exfiltration.
- Assess the security impact of the compromise.

### Evidence Sources

| Artifact | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `dump.eml` | Phishing email and attachment analysis |
| `powershell.json` | PowerShell execution and attacker activity |
| `capture.pcapng` | HTTP, DNS and network traffic analysis |

### Tools

Thunderbird, LNKParse3, jq, Wireshark, TShark, CyberChef, Linux command-line utilities and KeePass-compatible database software.

**Investigation Category:** Phishing Analysis / Endpoint Investigation / Network Forensics / Data Exfiltration

