## 3. Reconstructed Attack Sequence

This is a logical reconstruction based on the investigation artifacts. It is not a timestamp-verified event timeline.

| Stage | Attacker activity | Supporting evidence |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Delivered phishing email | `dump.eml` |
| 2 | Used an encrypted attachment containing a shortcut | `Invoice_20230103.lnk` |
| 3 | Triggered encoded PowerShell execution | LNK command-line arguments |
| 4 | Retrieved additional content | File-hosting domain |
| 5 | Enumerated the compromised system | Seatbelt activity |
| 6 | Accessed locally stored application data | `sq3.exe`, `plum.sqlite` |
| 7 | Communicated with C2 infrastructure | HTTP POST traffic |
| 8 | Exfiltrated a KeePass database | DNS queries containing hexadecimal data |
| 9 | Exposed sensitive information | Recovered database contents |

