## 7. Conclusion

The Boogeyman 1 investigation demonstrated how a phishing attachment can lead to a multi-stage compromise involving endpoint execution, system enumeration, command-and-control communication, and sensitive-data exfiltration.

By correlating email evidence, PowerShell execution logs, and packet capture data, the investigation reconstructed the attacker's behavior across multiple stages.

The most significant finding was the use of DNS queries to transfer hexadecimal-encoded data representing an encrypted KeePass database.

